{"name":"Vinaigrette","hex":"#efdaae","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vinaigrette","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sauce, made of an acidic liquid such as vinegar or lemon juice; oil; and other ingredients, used as a salad dressing, or as a marinade for cold meats.","A small perforated box for holding aromatic vinegar contained in a sponge, or a smelling bottle for smelling salts"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vinaigrette"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vinaigrette","blocks":[{"text":"Vinaigrette is a dressing made by mixing an edible oil with a mild acid such as vinegar or lemon juice. The mixture can be enhanced with salt, herbs and/or spices. It is used most commonly as a salad dressing, but can also be used as a marinade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Vinaigrette_dressing_with_a_chopped_salad.jpg/330px-Vinaigrette_dressing_with_a_chopped_salad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinaigrette","wikidata":"Q847441"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Making_vinaigrette.jpg/500px-Making_vinaigrette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Making_vinaigrette.jpg/1280px-Making_vinaigrette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Making_vinaigrette.jpg/500px-Making_vinaigrette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Making vinaigrette – pouring oil into vinegar and mustard prior to whipping into emulsion","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaking_vinaigrette.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Raspberry_vinaigrette.jpg/500px-Raspberry_vinaigrette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca